  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "Advanced verbs with fixed prepositions",
      "body": "At B2 you learned the common ones. These are typical of C1 texts:",
      "table": {
        "head": ["Verb", "Meaning", "Example"],
        "rows": [
          ["*carecer de*", "to lack", "*El proyecto carece de financiación.*"],
          ["*empeñarse en*", "to insist on / be set on", "*Se empeña en hacerlo solo.*"],
          ["*abstenerse de*", "to refrain from", "*Absténgase de fumar.*"],
          ["*prescindir de*", "to do without", "*No podemos prescindir de él.*"],
          ["*incurrir en*", "to incur / fall into", "*incurrir en un error, en gastos*"],
          ["*rebelarse contra*", "to rebel against", "*Se rebelaron contra el régimen.*"],
          ["*aferrarse a*", "to cling to", "*Se aferra al pasado.*"],
          ["*dignarse (a)*", "to deign to", "*Ni se dignó a contestar.*"],
          ["*jactarse de*", "to boast about", "*Se jacta de saberlo todo.*"],
          ["*desentenderse de*", "to wash your hands of", "*Se desentendió del asunto.*"],
          ["*percatarse de*", "to notice (formal)", "*No se percató del error.*"],
          ["*redundar en*", "to result in", "*Redundará en beneficio de todos.*"],
          ["*abogar por*", "to advocate for", "*Aboga por los derechos de los migrantes.*"],
          ["*hacer hincapié en*", "to stress / emphasize", "*Hizo hincapié en la seguridad.*"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "heading": "Same verb, different preposition, different meaning",
      "body": "*Acabar con* (to put an end to) vs. *acabar de* (to have just). *Dar con* (to find) vs. *dar a* (to face: *La ventana da al jardín*). *Contar con* (to count on) vs. *contar* (to tell). *Quedar con* (to meet someone) vs. *quedar en* (to agree on). *Hablar de* (to talk about) vs. *hablar con* (to talk to). *Pensar en* vs. *pensar de* (see B2)."
    }
  ],
